MASTER PROMPT — GLOBAL CASH MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (GCMS)

1. Project Overview

Build a complete enterprise-grade Global Cash Management System (GCMS) named Global Treasury & Cash Operations Platform.

The system must be designed for large multinational banking and corporate treasury environments, with capabilities comparable in functional scope to global transaction banking and treasury platforms used by institutions such as Citi, Wells Fargo, and Bank of America.

The application must support complex financial operations across:

* Multiple countries
* Multiple legal entities
* Parent and child entity hierarchies
* Multiple currencies
* Multiple bank accounts
* Multiple payment systems
* Multiple accounting ledgers
* Multiple business units
* Multiple time zones
* Multiple banking calendars

The application should be a fully functional enterprise application, not just a dashboard or UI prototype.

Implement all major modules, screens, workflows, APIs, data models, validations, accounting logic, reporting, exception handling, and operational controls.

Use realistic simulated financial data initially. The architecture must allow future integration with actual banking systems, payment processors, ERP platforms, SWIFT, and accounting systems.

Do not use proprietary source code, trademarks, or internal implementations from any specific bank. Build an original enterprise cash management platform with industry-standard functionality.

